    title: "[Bioinformatics & Multi-Omics Lane + Multi-Resolution Breast-Tumor Spatial Atlas + Endothelial Maturation Axis Linking Primed HEV to Mature TLS + Spatial-to-Single-Nucleus Resolution Bridging] GSE350571 'A cellular and vascular atlas of the breast tumor microenvironment with multi-resolution spatial transcriptomics [10x Xenium]' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=6, pdat 2026/11/03 = FRESHEST NOVEL accession band of the day, raw CSV + H5 + JSON + PARQUET + TIFF) + GSE351843 [10x Visium arm, score 6, n=40] + GSE351849 [10x Visium HD arm, score 6, n=4] + GSE351850 [SuperSeries, score 6, n=50] is the FIRST NOVEL multi-resolution breast-tumor vascular-atlas bundle of the archive; [Refractory-Cancer Lane + Solid-Tumour Acidosis Adaptation + Ceramide-Turnover Rewiring + Joint snRNA-seq plus snATAC-seq Multiome with Metacells, ARACNe3 Regulatory Networks and VIPER Activity Scoring] GSE352076 'Single-nucleus multiome (snRNA-seq + snATAC-seq) of MCF7 breast cancer cells under acute acidosis, chronic acid adaptation, and return to physiological pH' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=8, pdat 2026/11/03 = FRESHEST NOVEL accession band of the day, raw CSV + H5 + TBI + TSV) is the FIRST NOVEL acidosis-adaptation sphingolipid-rewiring multiome of the archive; [Clinical & Regulatory Lane + Humanized In-Vivo KMT2A-MLLT3 AML Model + CRISPR-Engineered KRAS G13D and G12C Subclonal Events + 20-Fold Leukemic-Stem-Cell Expansion + Emergent cDC1-Like Leukaemic Population + HARMONY Cohort Survival Confirmation] GSE300373 'Modelling KRAS Mutations in KMT2A-MLLT3 AML Promotes Leukemic Progression and Transcriptomic Remodeling' (Homo sapiens, score 6, n=23, pdat 2026/11/02, raw TXT, PubMed 42613434) is the FIRST NOVEL KRAS-subclonal-humanized KM3 AML dataset of the archive",
    category: "bioinformatics",
    summary: "Loop 001 daily digest for 2026-11-05, generated from research-watcher output/latest/hits.jsonl (109 hits across 27 query families, scan regenerated 2026-11-05 06:03 KST via 'bash run.sh scan', 0 source errors, hits.jsonl mtime 2026-11-05 06:03, collected_at 2026-11-04T21:02 UTC). The score-9 top band was ENTIRELY RECYCLED for the tenth consecutive cycle - the same GSE328275 TNBC-CD45 immune atlas, GSE328422 sequential lymph-node-metastasis spatial record, GSE326553 Oprm1-A118G opioid-dependence CosMx study, GSE346380 lung and GSE348495 colorectal CosMx resources, GSE288340 post-CAR-T marrow spatial atlas, GSE311507 HNSCC dependency map and the GSE281462/63/64/65 3D-chromatin-GWAS bundle that have topped every scan since early October - and the entire score-7 tier was either recycled (GSE314195/211/217 5hmC-5mC-scRNA mouse-brain bundle, published 2026-10-31) or outside BB's human-biomedical lanes (Ybx3 brown-adipocyte knockdown, nail-mesenchyme regeneration, TREM2 diabetic-nephropathy macrophages). The actionable harvest therefore came from the score-6 band, which for the first time in several cycles produced a genuine multi-platform bundle. Dedupe was performed at ACCESSION level against the FULL git history of src/app/digest/page.tsx, not merely against the visible 5-entry window: 'git log --all -S <GSE>' returned empty for every one of the three signals below, and a keyword-level cross-check confirmed that the biological SUBJECTS of all three signals (endothelial maturation and tertiary-lymphoid-structure organisation in breast tumour, ceramide-turnover rewiring under chronic acidosis in breast cancer cells, and KRAS-subclonal humanized KMT2A-MLLT3 acute myeloid leukaemia) have never been featured in any prior digest commit under any accession. Each signal was verified against its live NCBI GEO esummary record (title, depositor summary, taxon, sample count, pdat, gds_type, supplementary-file manifest, linked PubMed identifiers) rather than by title-matching alone. Signal 1 is the four-accession multi-resolution spatial bundle GSE350571 (Xenium, n=6), GSE351843 (Visium, n=40), GSE351849 (Visium HD, n=4) and GSE351850 (SuperSeries, n=50), all published 2026-11-03 and all part of one human breast-tumour study that profiles 33 tumour sections from 32 tumours plus 7 matched uninvolved lymph nodes, defining high endothelial venule states associated with tertiary lymphoid structures: a stromal 'primed' HEV state carrying STING-associated and adhesive programs, and a mature TLS-associated state additionally marked by lymphotoxin-beta receptor signalling, perivascular CCL19/CCL21 expression and SPP1, together defining a candidate endothelial maturation axis linked to TLS organisation. Signal 2 is GSE352076 (Homo sapiens, n=8, pdat 2026/11/03, CSV + H5 + TBI + TSV): joint single-nucleus RNA-seq and ATAC-seq multiome profiling of MCF7 breast cancer cells across four conditions - control at pH 7.4, acute acidosis at pH 6.5 for 3 days, chronic acid adaptation at pH 6.5 for more than 3 months, and return of acid-adapted cells to pH 7.4 for 3 days - showing that adaptation to acidosis is accompanied by plastic rewiring of sphingolipid metabolism centred on ceramide turnover, with transcriptionally similar nuclei aggregated into metacells, transcription-factor regulatory networks inferred with ARACNe3, and transcription-factor activity estimated with VIPER to score regulatory drive toward four ceramide clearance pathways (S1P, C1P, SM and GSL) and nominate candidate regulators of each. Signal 3 is GSE300373 (Homo sapiens, n=23, pdat 2026/11/02, TXT, PubMed 42613434): a humanized in vivo KMT2A-MLLT3 AML model in which KRAS G13D or G12C point mutations were introduced by CRISPR-Cas9 into CD34-positive cord-blood cells to mimic subclonal events observed in patients, showing that KRAS mutations significantly accelerate leukaemia onset and increase leukemic stem cell frequency by over 20-fold without altering the surface phenotype, with extensive transcriptional reprogramming including upregulation of stemness- and quiescence-associated genes such as IKZF2 and ALOX15, activation of inflammatory and NF-kappaB signalling, and - the key finding - a distinct population with a conventional type 1 dendritic cell (cDC1)-like transcriptional profile emerging exclusively in KRAS-mutated leukaemias and expressing key LSC regulators, with the HARMONY clinical cohort confirming significantly reduced overall survival in KM3 patients harbouring KRAS mutations. The unifying thesis of the day is THE AXIS IS THE UNIT OF INTERVENTION: in each dataset the actionable object is not a gene list but a graded axis with named endpoints and a measurable transition - a stromal endothelial maturation axis running from 'primed' HEV to mature TLS-associated HEV (Signal 1), a sphingolipid-clearance regulatory axis whose stability under chronic acid adaptation determines whether the rewiring is transient or plastic (Signal 2), and a leukaemic-progression axis on which a single subclonal KRAS event drives both stemness and the emergence of a new cell-state population (Signal 3). In each case BB's deliverable is a position on the axis plus the criterion that decides whether the subject is still movable, which continues the arc opened by id:146 (cell state as unit of prediction), id:145 (resolvable window), id:144 (earliest-resolvable state), id:143 (decision rule), id:142 (process boundary) and id:141 (axis resolution). A process note worth carrying forward: the score-9 band has now been fully saturated for ten consecutive cycles while the score-6 and score-4 bands carry the entire actionable harvest, and today's highest-value material was a MODALITY BUNDLE that the watcher's flat per-record scoring cannot express - the four spatial accessions of one study each scored only 6 individually, so a companion-bundle rule and a freshness-weighted score component are worth raising with the rubric owner rather than silently patching."